  "construction": "Two-block group-algebra code C(a,b) of arXiv:2610.13880 (Table 3) over the abelian group C15 x C3 (GAP SmallGroup(45,2)): H_X = (L(a) | R(b)), H_Z = (R(b)^T | L(a)^T) with L and R the left and right regular representations, a = 1 + x^6 + x^6 y + x^8 y^2 + x^10, b = 1 + x + x^8 y + x^10 y in generators x (order 15) and y (order 3), i.e. the bivariate bicycle code with A = a(x,y), B = b(x,y). The stored matrices use the qubit ordering of the paper's database (record 11f82b15fd82365c, github.com/gideonlsx/bicycle-race @ aed705a, data/codes.jsonl, CC BY 4.0): qubits 0..44 are the left block and 45..89 the right block, group elements numbered as GAP's Elements(SmallGroup(45,2)) with e0 the identity, x = e6, y = e2, so a = e0 + e1 + e3 + e8 + e41, b = e0 + e5 + e6 + e36. Rebuilt from the database's group data; CSS commutation, k, check weight and both of the paper's witnesses were re-checked on the rebuilt matrices.",
